direction: down

title: |md
  ## cgroup BPF and sockops
  per-cgroup network policy
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

cg_skb: "cgroup_skb" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  cg_body: |md
    Attach: cgroup_skb/{ingress,egress}

    Runs **per packet** for sockets in this cgroup.

    Returns:
    - 1 = allow
    - 0 = drop

    Per-cgroup network policy.

    Used by systemd, Cilium
    for network namespaces.

    Hook: cgroup_inet_egress
  |
}

sockops: "sock_ops" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  so_body: |md
    Runs at TCP **state events** (TCP_BPF_* callbacks):
    - TIMEOUT_INIT
    - RWND_INIT
    - HDR_OPT_LEN_CB
    - PARSE_HDR_OPT_CB
    - RTT_CB

    Tune connection params per cgroup:
    - RTO, recv window,
    - header options.

    Less common, very powerful.

    Hook: tcp_call_bpf
  |
}

sk_msg: "sk_msg" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  sm_body: |md
    Runs on **send** path of sockets in a sockmap.

    Can:
    - drop, redirect to another sock,
    - modify payload pre-sendmsg.

    Used for L7 LB and service mesh (sidecar offload).

    Hook: tcp_bpf_sendmsg
  |
}

cg_skb -> sockops -> sk_msg -> hook {style.stroke-dash: 4}

hook: "Each is a different\nnetwork-stack hook." {shape: text}
